PODSTGRESQL DBA PERFORMANCE SUMMARY FOR INETERVIEW - 


PostgreSQL DBA Tips
🧠 Tip 1: Kill problems early, not after outages
Most database “performance issues” are actually lock issues.
 Timeouts and guardrails protect production better than last-minute tuning.

🔒 Tip 2: Always look for blockers first
Before blaming slow queries, check what is waiting and who is blocking.
 One bad session can slow down the entire system.

🚨 Tip 3: Long transactions are silent killers
They lead to table bloat, delayed autovacuum, and unexpected downtime.
 If transactions stay open too long, problems pile up quietly.

⚙️ Tip 4: Use modern, future-proof designs
Adopting current PostgreSQL standards today avoids technical debt tomorrow.

📦 Tip 5: Vacuum is not optional
Ignoring cleanup is like never taking out the trash — eventually, things break.
 Healthy vacuuming keeps performance stable over time.

🧯 Tip 6: Fail fast during deployments
It’s better for a change to fail quickly than to freeze production systems.
 Fast failure saves teams from long outages.

📊 Tip 7: Monitoring beats tuning
If you’re not actively monitoring database activity and locks,
 you’re reacting too late instead of preventing issues.
 
 


