DBA Habits - 

How the Top 1% DBAs Plan Their Day

Ever wondered what separates an average DBA from the top 1%?

It’s not just certifications or years of experience, it’s how they structure their day 

1. Morning: Health Check First
– Review DB dashboards (CPU, memory, slow queries).
– Scan overnight alerts. Proactive beats firefighting.

2. Late Morning: Automate > Repeat
– Identify yesterday’s manual fixes.
– Script or automate them (Ansible, Terraform, Flyway).

3. Afternoon: Performance + Security
– Tuning slow queries, checking indexes.
– Reviewing access logs & user privileges (least privilege isn’t a buzzword).

4. Evening: Business Impact Mode
– Align with DevOps/Data teams.
– Ask: "How did the DB help business today? Faster insights? Reduced cost?"

5. Daily Habit: Learning 1 Thing
– Could be AWS Aurora failover, Postgres pg_partman, or Oracle AI Ops.
– Small learnings compound into massive growth.

The top DBAs don’t just "keep the lights on." They build trust, cut costs, and enable growth.

